            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3810/pgm.2011.03.2267</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary revascularization is a proven method to alleviate the symptoms of ischemic heart disease and improve survival. There have been many improvements in surgical revascularization since its advent &gt; 40 years ago and in balloon angioplasty since its first usage &gt; 30 years ago. Patients will continue to benefit as these surgical techniques continue to undergo further improvements. This article is a testament to the many physicians, surgeons, scientists, industry leaders, and insurers who continue to reinvent how we provide cutting-edge procedures in the most cost-effective manner for our patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
